.TH MODESWITCH 8 "2026" "realtek-usb-wifi-modeswitch 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
modeswitch \- switch Realtek USB Wi-Fi adapters out of CD-ROM mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modeswitch
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Many low-cost Realtek USB Wi-Fi adapters (RTL8192FU, RTL8821CU, RTL8811CU,
RTL8822BU, RTL8822CU and similar chips) enumerate as a USB CD-ROM drive when
they are first plugged in, so that Windows can auto-run the bundled driver.
Linux sees only the fake CD-ROM and the Wi-Fi function stays hidden until the
device is told to switch modes.
.PP
.B modeswitch
detects such devices, switches them to Wi-Fi mode with
.BR usb_modeswitch (1)
(a SCSI eject is used as a fallback), finds a kernel module that claims the
device's Wi-Fi USB ID, loads it, repairs bindings to the wrong driver and
optionally installs a udev rule that performs the switch automatically on
every plug-in.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Detect, switch mode, load a driver, install the udev rule and verify.
This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.B switch
Only switch devices from CD-ROM to Wi-Fi mode.
.TP
.B status
Show detected devices, modes, drivers and configuration. Does not need root.
.TP
.B list
List known install-mode product IDs.
.TP
.B clean
Remove the udev rule, blacklist and
.B usb_storage
quirk files used by this project (aliases: uninstall, --uninstall).
.TP
.B blacklist \fIMODULE\fR...
Prevent kernel module(s) from being auto-loaded.
.TP
.B unblacklist \fIMODULE\fR...
Undo
.BR blacklist .
.TP
.B help
Show help.
.TP
.B version
Show version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Answer yes to all questions (non-interactive).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Show what would be done without changing anything. May be used without root.
.TP
.B \-\-no-persist
Do not install the udev rule.
.TP
.B \-\-no-deps
Do not try to install missing packages.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid " PID"
Only handle the device with this product ID (4 hex digits; may be the CD-ROM
or the Wi-Fi mode ID, e.g. a192 or f192).
.TP
.BI \-\-message " HEX"
Use this switch message instead of the built-in one (wins over a
.B usb-modeswitch
config file).
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable colored output. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable is honoured as well.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force colored output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print debug information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-realtek-usb-wifi-modeswitch.rules
udev rule installed by
.BR "modeswitch setup" .
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/realtek-usb-wifi-modeswitch-blacklist.conf
Optional blacklist managed by
.BR "modeswitch blacklist" .
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/realtek-usb-wifi-modeswitch-usb-storage.conf
Optional
.B usb_storage
quirk that keeps the kernel from holding the fake CD-ROM (see the
troubleshooting guide); removed by
.BR "modeswitch clean" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo modeswitch
Run the full setup.
.TP
.B sudo modeswitch switch --pid a192
Switch one specific device.
.TP
.B modeswitch status
Inspect the system without root.
.TP
.B sudo modeswitch clean
Remove the udev rule, blacklist and usb-storage quirk.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH TESTED HARDWARE
The tool has been tested on Kylin V10 SP1 (kernel 5.15.0-72-generic) with a
generic OEM RTL8192FU 802.11n adapter: USB ID 0bda:a192 in CD-ROM mode,
0bda:f192 in Wi-Fi mode, bound to the out-of-tree 8192fu driver (module
8192fu, USB driver rtl8192fu). See the README for details.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usb_modeswitch (1),
.BR udev (7),
.BR nmcli (1)
